            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0581" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/1103a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-05T19:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1936—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>154. At request of Treasury Department, please report not later than morning of
                    June 8 information available at Shanghai in regard to the currency situation in
                    South China and the financial and monetary <pb facs="0582" n="487"
                        xml:id="pg487"/> aspects of the recent conference held at Canton between the
                    Nanking delegation and Southwest leaders.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
